From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:16:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Merge upstream dxvk-remix main of 2026-11-23
 (2b46bed0c..58ac72412)

Upstream NVIDIA dxvk-remix main at 58ac72412 ("Merge branch 'alpha-blend-dissolve-replacement-parts'
into 'main'"): 25 commits since 2b46bed0c, which patch 0093 merged. Merged with 2b46bed0c as the base
(a temporary graft of 0093's squashed commit onto it) and squashed into one commit. Upstream's fixes and
features come in whole: GPU and CPU crashes under VRAM pressure and invalid input (REMIX-6191), VRAM
logging and tracking, the merged BLAS no longer writing its transform into shared mesh geometry,
diffusion profile SSS on view-model geometry, fewer locks on the draw path (RtxOption reads, bridge and
DXVK thread pool critical sections, 64 command buffers per queue), faster texture budget lookups and
D3D9 light conversion, colour grading after either tonemapper, the alpha blend dissolve's 3D noise and
cutout for alpha-blended parts, particle birth masks, the revert of the GH:1112 translucent resolve
change, hand-authored NoSave options kept in saved layers (GH:798), SHaRC tweaks, the visible set
description for out-of-process consumers and an experimental GPU-resident scene for API hosts.

Where both sides changed the same lines:
- Remix API 0.1000.3: SceneInstanceAdd, SceneInstanceUpdate, SceneInstanceRemove and UpdateMaterial
  follow SetWaterSim and AddWaterDisturbance (slots 43-46, 376 bytes); the particle spawn mask is struct
  type 34 (33 upstream, the fork's PARTICLE_SCREEN_SIZE_EXT); a 0.1000.2 client is written its 344
  bytes, a 0.1000.0 or 0.1000.1 client its 328. docs/RemixApiChangelog.md has the entry.
- Device loss: any failed submission or fence wait ends the process, as upstream now does, through the
  fork's handleDeviceLost(reason), which calls onGpuCrash once; upstream's memory report follows it.
- Memory tracking: upstream's wasDemoted() with the fork's memory flags (host memory census).
- Option reads: a trivially copyable value is read from upstream's published copy (m_publishedValue,
  never torn) inside the fork's kLockFreeRead branch; the fork's resolved revision and hash set copies
  stay. An option layer's save keeps upstream's NoSave rule inside the fork's update-mutex copy.
- Texture categories keep the fork's TextureCategorySets (rtx_types.cpp, d3d9_rtx.cpp, d3d9_device.cpp);
  upstream's getTargetBuffer() takes the fork's effect colour rule.
- Upstream's option lock around the fixed-function stage loop in d3d9_device.cpp: the fork's texture category
  copies refresh before it is taken. Refreshed inside it, they locked the update mutex a second time on the same
  thread (it is not recursive): std::system_error (EDEADLK), a crash at the first draw after any option changed,
  found in the PoC. The stage loop in d3d9_rtx.cpp reads only the copies under its lock.
- View models: upstream's isViewModel material bit is texture flag bit 31 (22 upstream), since bits
  19-30 hold the MMD alpha cutoff.
- RTX IO: upstream's failed loads are kept until their reads complete and never published, with the
  fork's upload generations: a failed load is marked failed when it finalizes in the current generation.
  Hot reloads set asset data with upstream's setAssetData under the fork's asset info lock.
- Light replacements: upstream's per-frame light conversion cache with the fork's lookup logging.
- RtInstance keeps the fork's MMD alpha key beside upstream's original replacement index (832 bytes, with both
  sides' members in its copy constructor); the particle constants are 480 bytes (worldToProjection at 352): the fork's
  sceneTlasValid row and upstream's spawn context row.
- The fork has no local tonemapper: upstream's changes to it are left out; the global tonemapper
  keeps its colour grading controls, and the shader uses upstream's shared colorGrading, which clamps.
- The fork's test_memory_diagnostics (the memory log throttle) is test_memory_stats_data; upstream's
  memory diagnostics test keeps the name. The API test checks the 0.1000.2 and 0.1000.3 sizes; upstream's spawn mask
  test expects struct type 34.
- Left to the build: the spawn shader rejects a masked-out birth in the fork's SpawnSample form, upstream's
  getTargetBuffer() takes the fork's effect colour rule, and the GPU-resident scene's frame end calls the fork's
  manageTextureVram(ctx).
- RtxOptions.md is regenerated from the build (test_documentation): upstream's new options.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
